WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.940 --> 00:00:06.330
House of the Dragon Episode 8 is set six years
after the previous episode.

00:00:06.330 --> 00:00:12.469
So there are now new actors playing Rhaenyra’s
kids Jace Luke and Joff, and Daemon’s kids

00:00:12.469 --> 00:00:17.630
Baela and Rhaena, and Alicent’s kids Aegon,
Helaena and Aemond.

00:00:17.630 --> 00:00:22.730
Alicent’s family have been ruling in King’s
Landing, while Rhaenyra and her family have

00:00:22.730 --> 00:00:27.040
been living on Dragonstone, and Rhaenys and
Baela are on Driftmark.

00:00:27.040 --> 00:00:34.190
But now, as King Viserys and Lord Corlys both
seem near death, their families come together

00:00:34.190 --> 00:00:38.380
and try to make peace before it’s too late.

00:00:38.380 --> 00:00:40.420
So what happens and what does it mean?

00:00:40.420 --> 00:00:44.539
This video has no spoilers for Hot D past
episode 8.

00:00:44.539 --> 00:00:49.910
Rhaenys Targaryen has been ruling Driftmark,
the Velaryon island.

00:00:49.910 --> 00:00:54.999
Because her husband Lord Corlys Velaryon has
been at war on the Stepstones, fighting the

00:00:54.999 --> 00:00:56.030
Triarchy.

00:00:56.030 --> 00:01:02.870
Daemon killed the Triarchy’s leader the
Crabfeeder years ago, but this war continues.

00:01:02.870 --> 00:01:07.300
And now Corlys is wounded, and it seems he
might die.

00:01:07.300 --> 00:01:12.370
In the books, Corlys isn’t wounded, he just
gets sick because he’s old – Corlys is

00:01:12.370 --> 00:01:15.510
now seventy-six years old in the books.

00:01:15.510 --> 00:01:21.900
So Corlys’ brother Vaemond asks who will
be the next Lord of Driftmark if Corlys dies.

00:01:21.900 --> 00:01:27.760
Corlys wants Lucerys Velaryon to inherit Driftmark,
cause Luke is supposedly the son of Laenor

00:01:27.760 --> 00:01:28.940
Velaryon.

00:01:28.940 --> 00:01:34.490
But Vaemond says that since Luke is actually
Harwin Strong’s bastard, Vaemond should

00:01:34.490 --> 00:01:36.720
get Driftmark.

00:01:36.720 --> 00:01:42.260
While Rhaenys previously said that she wants
her granddaughter Baela to inherit Driftmark.

00:01:42.260 --> 00:01:48.140
So this begins a power struggle between Luke,
Vaemond and Baela to control the second most

00:01:48.140 --> 00:01:50.770
powerful house in Westeros, House Velaryon.

00:01:50.770 --> 00:01:56.680
On Dragonstone, Daemon and Rhaenyra now have
two sons named Aegon and Viserys.

00:01:56.680 --> 00:02:02.420
Daemon has settled into married life, and
just as Viserys’ dad hobby was his model

00:02:02.420 --> 00:02:06.280
city, Daemon’s hobby is collecting dragon
eggs.

00:02:06.280 --> 00:02:12.950
Daemon climbs around the Dragonmont, a volcanic
mountain on Dragonstone, and he finds some

00:02:12.950 --> 00:02:16.780
dragon eggs laid by Rhaenyra’s dragon Syrax.

00:02:16.780 --> 00:02:22.080
The eggs are laid in a sack that’s hard
on the outside and warm on the inside, it

00:02:22.080 --> 00:02:27.120
looks like the eggs in the movie Alien, and
apparently this is how dragon eggs incubate

00:02:27.120 --> 00:02:28.240
in the wild.

00:02:28.240 --> 00:02:32.820
Daemon takes the eggs to put in a “warming
chamber”, maybe he’ll give them to his

00:02:32.820 --> 00:02:34.860
new sons.

00:02:34.860 --> 00:02:39.340
Dragons are weapons, and Daemon is stockpiling
eggs for future conflict – like an apocalypse

00:02:39.340 --> 00:02:40.340
prepper filling a bunker with fire-breathing
nukes.

00:02:40.340 --> 00:02:45.390
Daemon’s Dragonkeepers have blood and burns
on their faces – looks like wrangling dragons

00:02:45.390 --> 00:02:47.420
is a dangerous job.

00:02:47.420 --> 00:02:51.900
Rhaenyra’s eldest son Jace practices speaking
Valyrian.

00:02:51.900 --> 00:02:56.160
He says that Aegon the Conqueror ordered for
some trees to be felled.

00:02:56.160 --> 00:03:02.099
Cause when Aegon landed on Westeros he cleared
away forest to build what eventually became

00:03:02.099 --> 00:03:04.150
the city of King’s Landing.

00:03:04.150 --> 00:03:09.380
He didn’t cut down every tree though – there’s
still that weirwood tree in the Red Keep,

00:03:09.380 --> 00:03:11.350
sacred to the old gods.

00:03:11.350 --> 00:03:17.520
Jace is the heir to the Throne after Rhaenyra,
so he studies hard, and takes his responsibilities

00:03:17.520 --> 00:03:18.740
seriously.

00:03:18.740 --> 00:03:24.850
Unlike Alicent’s eldest son Aegon, who takes
nothing seriously except for masturbation.

00:03:24.850 --> 00:03:30.880
We see the Painted Table, a map of Westeros
that Aegon made before his Conquest.

00:03:30.880 --> 00:03:35.540
Stannis and Daenerys use this same table later
in Game of Thrones.

00:03:35.540 --> 00:03:39.570
Rhaenyra and Daemon learn that Vaemond wants
to take Driftmark instead of Luke.

00:03:39.570 --> 00:03:44.890
If Luke is disinherited for being a bastard,
that could weaken Jace and Rhaenyra’s claims

00:03:44.890 --> 00:03:46.220
to the Throne.

00:03:46.220 --> 00:03:50.560
And if Luke doesn’t get Driftmark, their
family won’t get the Velaryons’ wealth

00:03:50.560 --> 00:03:52.680
and powerful ships.

00:03:52.680 --> 00:03:58.069
So Rhaenyra and her family go back to King’s
Landing to defend their power.

00:03:58.069 --> 00:04:03.510
Rhaenyra doesn’t get a big official welcome
to the Keep – Otto specifically keeps it

00:04:03.510 --> 00:04:08.270
low-key to undermine Rhaenyra, and make her
seem less important.

00:04:08.270 --> 00:04:12.720
Kinda like Viserys’ welcome to Driftmark
previously.

00:04:12.720 --> 00:04:19.230
Rhaenyra is greeted only by Lord Allun Caswell
– we saw him previously congratulating Rhaenyra

00:04:19.230 --> 00:04:20.840
after childbirth.

00:04:20.840 --> 00:04:26.600
House Caswell have a centaur for a sigil and
they rule Bitterbridge in the Reach.

00:04:26.600 --> 00:04:31.040
Rhaenyra and Daemon find that the Red Keep
has changed while they were gone.

00:04:31.040 --> 00:04:36.440
Alicent and Otto have taken down Targaryen
heraldry, and covered up those dragon orgy

00:04:36.440 --> 00:04:40.630
murals, and replaced them with symbols of
the Faith of the Seven.

00:04:40.630 --> 00:04:45.880
The showrunners say that Alicent turns to
religion to redeem herself after she attacked

00:04:45.880 --> 00:04:48.050
Rhaenyra last episode.

00:04:48.050 --> 00:04:50.220
But this is also a political move.

00:04:50.220 --> 00:04:55.820
Cause the Faith is closely tied to the power
of House Hightower – the Faith is based

00:04:55.820 --> 00:04:58.750
in the Hightower city of Oldtown.

00:04:58.750 --> 00:05:04.639
These religious symbols may imply disapproval
of Rhaenyra’s incestuous marriage with Daemon,

00:05:04.639 --> 00:05:06.760
and of her bastard children.

00:05:06.760 --> 00:05:12.070
The removal of Targaryen imagery shows that
the Targaryens aren’t in charge here – Otto

00:05:12.070 --> 00:05:15.389
and Alicent Hightower control the Throne.

00:05:15.389 --> 00:05:20.800
Rhaenyra and Daemon go visit Viserys, and
see that Viserys’ model city is now covered

00:05:20.800 --> 00:05:23.930
in cobwebs, there’s even a rat on it.

00:05:23.930 --> 00:05:28.560
Viserys is so sick that he’s no longer working
on his passion project.

00:05:28.560 --> 00:05:34.230
And the neglected dirty city suggests that
Viserys’ kingdom is corrupt, his realm is

00:05:34.230 --> 00:05:35.460
disordered.

00:05:35.460 --> 00:05:41.949
The smoke amidst the city evokes the smoking
ruin of Valyria after its downfall.

00:05:41.949 --> 00:05:45.199
Viserys’ sickness is something like leprosy.

00:05:45.199 --> 00:05:51.639
He’s in constant pain, body parts are falling
off, and part of his face is now gone.

00:05:51.639 --> 00:05:58.320
Daemon has always looked to Viserys for approval
and love, so he’s so devastated to see his

00:05:58.320 --> 00:06:02.520
brother dying that Daemon can hardly look
at Viserys.

00:06:02.520 --> 00:06:07.160
Rhaenyra shows Viserys his new grandsons – Aegon
and Viserys.

00:06:07.160 --> 00:06:10.380
Viserys is named after King Viserys.

00:06:10.380 --> 00:06:13.360
And Aegon is named after Aegon the Conqueror.

00:06:13.360 --> 00:06:17.270
Of course, Alicent already has a son named
Aegon.

00:06:17.270 --> 00:06:22.570
The books say that Rhaenyra named her kid
Aegon the same name to insult Alicent.

00:06:22.570 --> 00:06:28.530
And it also shows Rhaenyra’s political ambitions
– naming her kids after King Viserys and

00:06:28.530 --> 00:06:33.760
King Aegon suggests that Rhaenyra’s children
are the true royal bloodline.

00:06:33.760 --> 00:06:39.050
Unlike Jace, Luke and Joff, who are obviously
Harwin’s bastards because of their dark

00:06:39.050 --> 00:06:45.890
hair, Aegon and Viserys have Targaryen blonde
hair – they look like kings.

00:06:45.890 --> 00:06:49.740
And Rhaenyra is now pregnant again with her
sixth child.

00:06:49.740 --> 00:06:55.010
Viserys is happy to meet his new grandkids,
though the grandkids are less happy to meet

00:06:55.010 --> 00:06:56.010
him.

00:06:56.010 --> 00:07:01.430
When Viserys is overwhelmed with pain, he
drinks milk of the poppy, which is basically

00:07:01.430 --> 00:07:03.570
opium, a painkiller.

00:07:03.570 --> 00:07:08.580
So Viserys is drugged out of his mind half
the time, and lets Alicent and Otto run the

00:07:08.580 --> 00:07:10.180
kingdom for him.

00:07:10.180 --> 00:07:15.930
So Rhaenyra and Daemon think Viserys will
be no help with the Driftmark succession issue.

00:07:15.930 --> 00:07:21.040
Alicent and Otto run a small council meeting,
dealing with such thrilling issues as the

00:07:21.040 --> 00:07:23.150
taxation of wool.

00:07:23.150 --> 00:07:27.449
Viserys once said that Daemon could never
be king because he’d find the actual work

00:07:27.449 --> 00:07:29.789
of government to be boring.

00:07:29.789 --> 00:07:34.520
If he had to sit at a table every day putting
up with all this bullshit, Daemon would go

00:07:34.520 --> 00:07:35.520
mad.

00:07:35.520 --> 00:07:39.910
But Alicent and Otto have the patience, and
are doing the work.

00:07:39.910 --> 00:07:43.800
Though they’re also scheming for their own
ambitions.

00:07:43.800 --> 00:07:47.340
Alicent speaks with a Kingsguard called Erryk
Cargyll.

00:07:47.340 --> 00:07:52.750
Erryk has a twin brother called Arryk who’s
also a Kingsguard, and Alicent can’t tell

00:07:52.750 --> 00:07:54.780
Erryk and Arryk apart.

00:07:54.780 --> 00:07:59.790
Also on the Kingsguard is Commander Harrold
Westerling, Criston Cole, Steffon Darklyn,

00:07:59.790 --> 00:08:02.190
and two others we haven’t met yet.

00:08:02.190 --> 00:08:07.250
Alicent learns that her son Prince Aegon raped
a servant called Dyana.

00:08:07.250 --> 00:08:11.539
Dyana is traumatised, and terrified that she’ll
be punished.

00:08:11.539 --> 00:08:17.310
In this world, we see many women punished
or killed for having sex with the wrong person,

00:08:17.310 --> 00:08:18.310
even if they didn’t choose to.

00:08:18.310 --> 00:08:19.390
Some women are labelled whores or sinners.

00:08:19.390 --> 00:08:24.710
A noble girl who has sex outside wedlock might
be hastily married someplace, or sent away

00:08:24.710 --> 00:08:26.560
to be a sister of the faith.

00:08:26.560 --> 00:08:32.889
But lowborn girls like Dyana may be considered
permanently tarnished, labelled as whores

00:08:32.889 --> 00:08:34.039
or sinners.

00:08:34.039 --> 00:08:36.490
Alicent comforts Dyana.

00:08:36.490 --> 00:08:41.210
Maybe she relates to Dyana, because Alicent
experienced Viserys having sex with her when

00:08:41.210 --> 00:08:42.909
she didn’t want to.

00:08:42.909 --> 00:08:48.750
But Alicent also subtly threatens Dyana, and
pays her so that she won’t tell anyone that

00:08:48.750 --> 00:08:50.390
Aegon raped her.

00:08:50.390 --> 00:08:55.690
Alicent presents her family as the religious
and virtuous royals, so she doesn’t want

00:08:55.690 --> 00:08:58.990
rumours of Aegon’s crimes shaming her family.

00:08:58.990 --> 00:09:04.700
And she doesn’t want rumours of potential
royal bastards who might become rival claimants

00:09:04.700 --> 00:09:05.980
for the Throne.

00:09:05.980 --> 00:09:11.360
So on one level, Alicent supports Dyana, but
at the same time Alicent silences Dyana and

00:09:11.360 --> 00:09:14.050
protects Aegon’s reputation.

00:09:14.050 --> 00:09:19.260
Rhaenyra previously said that Alicent wears
a “cloak” of “righteousness” – like,

00:09:19.260 --> 00:09:26.540
her image as a righteous virtuous woman is
a fake disguise to hide her family’s corruption.

00:09:26.540 --> 00:09:32.190
Alicent participates in enforcing the same
patriarchal system that had trapped her.

00:09:32.190 --> 00:09:38.279
Alicent gives Dyana moon tea to prevent pregnancy,
like when Rhaenyra had moon tea.

00:09:38.279 --> 00:09:43.560
Mellos said that moon tea can be “unpleasant”
if brewed improperly.

00:09:43.560 --> 00:09:47.850
In the books, Lysa Tully almost dies from
drinking moon tea.

00:09:47.850 --> 00:09:50.620
So hopefully Dyana’s okay.

00:09:50.620 --> 00:09:55.090
Alicent confronts Aegon, and shouts at him
for raping Dyana.

00:09:55.090 --> 00:10:01.149
Alicent seems more concerned about the political
consequences of the rape than about its immorality.

00:10:01.149 --> 00:10:04.880
Alicent slaps Aegon, as she did last episode.

00:10:04.880 --> 00:10:09.870
Alicent’s parenting of Aegon involves a
lot of shouting and hitting, and this has

00:10:09.870 --> 00:10:12.600
not made Aegon a better person.

00:10:12.600 --> 00:10:18.080
Alicent is disgusted by him, and tells Aegon
“You're no son of mine”.

00:10:18.080 --> 00:10:21.769
Tywin says the same thing to Tyrion in Game
of Thrones.

00:10:21.769 --> 00:10:26.550
And we see in Tyrion the pain that is caused
by a parent’s rejection.

00:10:26.550 --> 00:10:30.670
Aegon doesn’t get much love from his father
Viserys either.

00:10:30.670 --> 00:10:36.830
Maybe Aegon’s feelings of rejection fuel
his cruel behaviour, expressing his pain by

00:10:36.830 --> 00:10:37.830
hurting others.

00:10:37.830 --> 00:10:40.839
Kinda like Tyrion in the later books.

00:10:40.839 --> 00:10:45.279
Alicent hugs Helaena, who is Aegon’s sister
and wife.

00:10:45.279 --> 00:10:49.600
Aegon and Helaena now have two young children
who we haven’t seen yet.

00:10:49.600 --> 00:10:55.510
And Alicent feels terrible for Helaena being
married to this useless cheating rapist.

00:10:55.510 --> 00:10:59.769
Even though the Hightowers’ political ambitions
are probably why Aegon and Helaena got married

00:10:59.769 --> 00:11:01.360
in the first place.

00:11:01.360 --> 00:11:05.530
Alicent faces Rhaenyra and Daemon after long
years apart.

00:11:05.530 --> 00:11:10.260
We see the scar on Rhaenyra’s arm where
Alicent slashed her last episode.

00:11:10.260 --> 00:11:15.440
And two sides remain prickly and passive aggressive
with each other.

00:11:15.440 --> 00:11:20.910
Rhaenyra says Alicent and Otto are deliberately
keeping Viserys weak and drugged so that they

00:11:20.910 --> 00:11:23.149
can rule in Viserys’ name.

00:11:23.149 --> 00:11:27.230
But Alicent argues that Viserys needs the
drugs for his pain, and that the Hightowers

00:11:27.230 --> 00:11:29.850
are doing the right thing.

00:11:29.850 --> 00:11:32.310
Jace and Luke visit the training yard.

00:11:32.310 --> 00:11:36.860
They remember one time when Luke tried to
use Criston’s morningstar, and almost hit

00:11:36.860 --> 00:11:38.480
himself in the head.

00:11:38.480 --> 00:11:42.721
Criston’s actor says that he was more worried
about hitting himself in the balls, which

00:11:42.721 --> 00:11:46.700
was quote “not cool” and “not rock and
roll”.

00:11:46.700 --> 00:11:52.140
Luke is uncomfortable being here to claim
Driftmark, knowing that he’s not Laenor

00:11:52.140 --> 00:11:56.170
Velaryon’s son, that he looks like his real
father Harwin.

00:11:56.170 --> 00:12:02.420
This young man is forced to lie about his
identity for the sake of his parents’ politics.

00:12:02.420 --> 00:12:06.660
Jace supports his brother by saying it doesn’t
matter what other people think.

00:12:06.660 --> 00:12:10.709
Which sounds nice, but.. it’s really not
true.

00:12:10.709 --> 00:12:13.000
Politics is all about what people think.

00:12:13.000 --> 00:12:18.300
And if no one believes in Luke’s legitimacy,
he won’t survive as a ruler.

00:12:18.300 --> 00:12:22.180
We see Aemond Targaryen training with Criston
Cole.

00:12:22.180 --> 00:12:27.290
The books say that with Criston’s training,
Aemond became a “proficient and dangerous

00:12:27.290 --> 00:12:30.080
swordsman”, despite the loss of his eye.

00:12:30.080 --> 00:12:33.810
Criston says Aemond will win tournaments with
his skill.

00:12:33.810 --> 00:12:36.490
But Aemond says he doesn’t care about tourneys.

00:12:36.490 --> 00:12:40.720
Aemond only cares about real fights, real
killing.

00:12:40.720 --> 00:12:43.209
Then he looks at Jace and Luke.

00:12:43.209 --> 00:12:48.140
Luke cut out Aemond’s eye last episode,
and Aemond wants revenge.

00:12:48.140 --> 00:12:54.070
Vaemond Velaryon marches in surrounded by
Velaryon and Hightower heraldry.

00:12:54.070 --> 00:12:59.140
Vaemond knows that in politics “what other
people think” is everything.

00:12:59.140 --> 00:13:05.350
So he presents himself as the true Velaryon
heir, with House Hightower’s support.

00:13:05.350 --> 00:13:10.660
Otto and Alicent meet with Vaemond, and Otto
says there may be war soon.

00:13:10.660 --> 00:13:15.350
He means that the Triarchy on the Stepstones
could become a threat to Westeros, but he

00:13:15.350 --> 00:13:19.959
also thinks there could be war between Rhaenyra
and Aegon for the Throne.

00:13:19.959 --> 00:13:24.080
Which is largely Otto’s fault for pushing
Aegon as heir.

00:13:24.080 --> 00:13:28.890
To prepare for war, the Hightowers want the
support of House Velaryon, with their money

00:13:28.890 --> 00:13:29.890
and ships.

00:13:29.890 --> 00:13:34.980
Vaemond says that if they help him inherit
Driftmark, Vaemond will support the Hightowers.

00:13:34.980 --> 00:13:40.700
Once they disinherit Luke, Otto hopes to disinherit
Jace and Rhaenyra, and to put his grandson

00:13:40.700 --> 00:13:42.329
Aegon on the Throne.

00:13:42.329 --> 00:13:44.370
But Alicent has doubts.

00:13:44.370 --> 00:13:49.000
She’s not sure if she wants to go against
Corlys and Viserys’ wishes.

00:13:49.000 --> 00:13:53.850
And does she really want her terrible son
Aegon to be king?

00:13:53.850 --> 00:13:59.269
While the Hightowers make an alliance with
Vaemond, Rhaenyra tries to ally with Rhaenys.

00:13:59.269 --> 00:14:04.310
Rhaenys is happy to see her granddaughter
Rhaena, who has been living on Dragonstone

00:14:04.310 --> 00:14:05.750
with Rhaenyra and Daemon.

00:14:05.750 --> 00:14:08.840
But Rhaenys is cold to Rhaenyra.

00:14:08.840 --> 00:14:14.209
She’s always been a bit hostile to Rhaenyra,
maybe envious that Rhaenyra is heir to the

00:14:14.209 --> 00:14:17.620
Throne when Rhaenys herself was rejected from
the Throne.

00:14:17.620 --> 00:14:23.380
But now Rhaenys is really mad because she
believes that Rhaenyra killed her son Laenor

00:14:23.380 --> 00:14:28.960
– and apparently Rhaenyra has just let Rhaenys
believe that for the last six years.

00:14:28.960 --> 00:14:35.050
Rhaenys wears black clothes, as though she’s
still mourning the deaths of her children.

00:14:35.050 --> 00:14:39.880
Rhaenyra now says that she didn’t kill Laenor,
but she doesn’t reveal that Laenor is in

00:14:39.880 --> 00:14:42.329
fact still alive in the east somewhere.

00:14:42.329 --> 00:14:47.170
She wants to respect Laenor’s choice to
be free and anonymous.

00:14:47.170 --> 00:14:49.600
And Rhaenyra proposes an alliance.

00:14:49.600 --> 00:14:55.470
If Rhaenys supports Luke’s claim to Driftmark,
then Luke will marry Rhaena, and Jace will

00:14:55.470 --> 00:14:56.740
marry Baela.

00:14:56.740 --> 00:15:00.550
So when Jace becomes King of Westeros, Baela
will be queen.

00:15:00.550 --> 00:15:05.089
And when Luke becomes Lord of Driftmark, Rhaena
will be Lady of Driftmark.

00:15:05.089 --> 00:15:10.420
This alliance would make Rhaenys’ granddaughters
two of the most powerful women in Westeros.

00:15:10.420 --> 00:15:15.790
But Rhaenys has said before that she’s more
interested in keeping her family safe than

00:15:15.790 --> 00:15:18.070
she wants political power.

00:15:18.070 --> 00:15:23.100
If the Hightowers bring down Rhaenyra, Rhaenys
doesn’t want to go down with her.

00:15:23.100 --> 00:15:28.220
So Rhaenys rejects Rhaenyra’s offer, and
says she’ll stand alone.

00:15:28.220 --> 00:15:33.779
We hear thunder in the background, which evokes
the storm of war that’s coming.

00:15:33.779 --> 00:15:39.520
And reminds us that Rhaenys’ mother was
Jocelyn Baratheon of Storm’s End, the castle

00:15:39.520 --> 00:15:42.279
that withstands the storm.

00:15:42.279 --> 00:15:45.089
So Rhaenyra feels alone and afraid.

00:15:45.089 --> 00:15:49.180
Without allies, she can’t protect her family.

00:15:49.180 --> 00:15:52.690
Rhaenyra visits Viserys, and asks him to defend
her.

00:15:52.690 --> 00:15:57.860
Viserys had told Rhaenyra about the prophecy
of Aegon the Conqueror, that the Targaryens

00:15:57.860 --> 00:16:01.270
must be united to save the world from the
white walkers.

00:16:01.270 --> 00:16:08.010
But by making Rhaenyra his heir, then allowing
Alicent and Otto to take power, Viserys has

00:16:08.010 --> 00:16:09.890
divided and weakened his family.

00:16:09.890 --> 00:16:13.430
He’s failing as a king and as a father.

00:16:13.430 --> 00:16:17.639
In the morning, we see how Viserys’ sickness
has ravaged his body.

00:16:17.639 --> 00:16:19.750
We see the pain he’s in.

00:16:19.750 --> 00:16:23.380
But today, Viserys refuses to drink the milk
of the poppy drug.

00:16:23.380 --> 00:16:29.730
He wants his mind clear, so he can finally
fix the political divide in his family.

00:16:29.730 --> 00:16:33.800
In the books, Viserys doesn’t have this
terrible leprosy disease.

00:16:33.800 --> 00:16:39.130
Viserys just has a weak heart cause he’s
fat and drinks too much, and he cuts his hand

00:16:39.130 --> 00:16:40.579
on the Iron Throne.

00:16:40.579 --> 00:16:44.360
The books say that Viserys is just not that
interested in politics.

00:16:44.360 --> 00:16:51.430
But in the show, Viserys has good intentions,
he does care, he just makes bad mistakes,

00:16:51.430 --> 00:16:54.300
and eventually gets too sick and weak.

00:16:54.300 --> 00:16:59.490
The author of the books George Martin says
that the Viserys in Hot D is a much better

00:16:59.490 --> 00:17:04.480
and more tragic character than the Viserys
in the books – so much so that George feels

00:17:04.480 --> 00:17:06.860
tempted to rewrite his books.

00:17:06.860 --> 00:17:12.769
Otto holds court as Hand of the King to decide
who’ll inherit Driftmark after Corlys.

00:17:12.769 --> 00:17:18.399
Of course, Otto has already agreed to give
Driftmark to Vaemond, so this is just empty

00:17:18.399 --> 00:17:22.019
political theatre, a cloak of righteousness.

00:17:22.019 --> 00:17:28.069
Vaemond speaks of the history of House Velaryon,
how they are one of the only surviving families

00:17:28.069 --> 00:17:32.600
from Old Valyria, how they’ve been allies
of the Targaryens for centuries.

00:17:32.600 --> 00:17:40.730
Vaemond says he has true Velaryon blood – implying
that Luke is a bastard, and not a real Velaryon.

00:17:40.730 --> 00:17:46.850
Before Otto can give Driftmark to Vaemond,
King Viserys unexpectedly turns up.

00:17:46.850 --> 00:17:53.359
He walks slowly and painfully to the Throne,
making this huge effort to support his daughter

00:17:53.359 --> 00:17:55.429
Rhaenyra and her family.

00:17:55.429 --> 00:18:00.659
Viserys’ brother Daemon helps him to his
throne and puts his crown back on his head

00:18:00.659 --> 00:18:02.359
when it falls off.

00:18:02.359 --> 00:18:07.490
It wasn’t in the script for Viserys’ crown
to fall off – that just happened accidentally,

00:18:07.490 --> 00:18:08.979
and the actors went with it.

00:18:08.979 --> 00:18:14.730
It’s a touching moment of love and support
between brothers with a rough history.

00:18:14.730 --> 00:18:19.980
In Episode 1, it was hinted that Daemon might
kill Viserys to take his crown.

00:18:19.980 --> 00:18:25.539
But even after all the fights and exiles,
Daemon is loyal to his brother.

00:18:25.539 --> 00:18:31.859
Viserys says this whole Velaryon succession
question was already settled – Lord Corlys

00:18:31.859 --> 00:18:34.389
wants Luke to inherit Driftmark.

00:18:34.389 --> 00:18:35.649
And Rhaenys agrees.

00:18:35.649 --> 00:18:39.399
Earlier, Rhaenys had said she wouldn’t support
Luke.

00:18:39.399 --> 00:18:45.000
But now she does, and agrees to Rhaenyra’s
proposal to marry Luke to Rhaena and Jace

00:18:45.000 --> 00:18:46.000
to Baela.

00:18:46.000 --> 00:18:47.000
So Rhaena will be Lady of Driftmark, and Baela
will be Jace’s queen.

00:18:47.000 --> 00:18:51.070
It’s a pretty good compromise, really – cause
Rhaena and Luke’s children will have Velaryon

00:18:51.070 --> 00:18:53.359
blood through Rhaena’s mother Laena.

00:18:53.359 --> 00:18:58.220
So if Vaemond really just cares about the
Velaryon bloodline, he should be okay with

00:18:58.220 --> 00:19:00.929
Luke and Rhaena taking Driftmark.

00:19:00.929 --> 00:19:03.649
But Vaemond wants the power for himself.

00:19:03.649 --> 00:19:09.450
Viserys calls Vaemond a second son, which
reminds us that Vaemond may feel frustrated

00:19:09.450 --> 00:19:14.220
that he’s always been less powerful than
his big brother Lord Corlys.

00:19:14.220 --> 00:19:19.179
And Vaemond’s angry about the lies, that
everyone’s pretending that Luke is Laenor’s

00:19:19.179 --> 00:19:21.899
son when he’s really Harwin’s bastard.

00:19:21.899 --> 00:19:27.539
So Vaemond finally shouts the truth – that
Rhaenyra’s sons are “bastards” – and

00:19:27.539 --> 00:19:29.740
he calls Rhaenyra a “whore”.

00:19:29.740 --> 00:19:32.480
Vaemond knows that he’ll be punished for
this.

00:19:32.480 --> 00:19:37.330
Vaemond’s actor says Vaemond falls on his
sword to tell the truth.

00:19:37.330 --> 00:19:41.649
Suddenly, Daemon cuts through Vaemond’s
head.

00:19:41.649 --> 00:19:48.019
The cut is so clean because Daemon uses his
Valyrian steel sword Dark Sister, and Valyrian

00:19:48.019 --> 00:19:50.200
steel is super sharp.

00:19:50.200 --> 00:19:53.139
In the books, Vaemond’s death is different.

00:19:53.139 --> 00:19:58.240
Rhaenyra orders Daemon to kill Vaemond, and
then Rhaenyra feeds Vaemond’s corpse to

00:19:58.240 --> 00:19:59.690
her dragon.

00:19:59.690 --> 00:20:03.690
So Rhaenyra seems more villainous in the books
here.

00:20:03.690 --> 00:20:08.279
Vaemond’s corpse is.. reassembled by the
silent sisters.

00:20:08.279 --> 00:20:12.960
The silent sisters are an order of women in
the Faith of the Seven who prepare the dead

00:20:12.960 --> 00:20:14.259
for the grave.

00:20:14.259 --> 00:20:18.659
They wear grey, and swear vows of chastity
and silence.

00:20:18.659 --> 00:20:23.090
They’re called “Death’s handmaidens”,
or “the Stranger’s wives” – cause

00:20:23.090 --> 00:20:26.419
the Stranger is the god of death in the Faith.

00:20:26.419 --> 00:20:32.659
The sisters cover their face because it’s
“ill fortune to look on the face of death”.

00:20:32.659 --> 00:20:38.049
But Rhaenys watches as the sisters prepare
the corpse of her brother-in-law.

00:20:38.049 --> 00:20:42.710
She says the Stranger has visited her more
times than she can count.

00:20:42.710 --> 00:20:49.639
Her daughter Laena died, her son Laenor seemingly
died, her husband Corlys may soon die.

00:20:49.639 --> 00:20:54.999
And if this conflict between Rhaenyra and
Alicent gets worse, many more people will

00:20:54.999 --> 00:20:55.999
die.

00:20:55.999 --> 00:21:01.380
By siding with Rhaenyra, Rhaenys has put herself
and her grandkids in danger.

00:21:01.380 --> 00:21:06.149
The royal family have dinner, and the showrunners
took inspiration here from the Last Supper

00:21:06.149 --> 00:21:08.229
painting by da Vinci.

00:21:08.229 --> 00:21:11.750
Rhaenyra and Alicent sit apart from each other.

00:21:11.750 --> 00:21:15.210
Which contrasts with how close they were in
the past.

00:21:15.210 --> 00:21:18.729
This shot is based on an illustration in the
book Fire &amp; Blood.

00:21:18.729 --> 00:21:24.529
Viserys holds this dinner to try to reunite
his family before he dies.

00:21:24.529 --> 00:21:28.549
In the throne room, Viserys used his strength
as king.

00:21:28.549 --> 00:21:33.659
But now, Viserys shows his vulnerability as
a father and a husband.

00:21:33.659 --> 00:21:39.480
He takes off his mask to show his withered
face, and urges his family to make peace for

00:21:39.480 --> 00:21:43.340
his sake as a dying old man who loves them.

00:21:43.340 --> 00:21:48.610
Rhaenyra is moved by her father’s words,
so Rhaenyra thanks Alicent for loving and

00:21:48.610 --> 00:21:51.109
supporting Viserys all these years.

00:21:51.109 --> 00:21:57.440
Alicent finds common ground with Rhaenyra,
and says Rhaenyra will be a good queen.

00:21:57.440 --> 00:22:02.989
And that startles Otto, cause his whole plan
is to make Aegon king instead of Rhaenyra.

00:22:02.989 --> 00:22:09.360
But Alicent and Rhaenyra really try to reconcile,
so for a moment it seems like peace is possible.

00:22:09.360 --> 00:22:14.279
But Rhaenyra and Alicent’s children continue
their conflict.

00:22:14.279 --> 00:22:16.671
Aegon insults Jace and his betrothed, Baela.

00:22:16.671 --> 00:22:18.197
But Jace does the mature thing, and speaks
of friendship with Aegon and Aemond.

00:22:18.197 --> 00:22:21.909
Helaena whispers another cryptic prediction.

00:22:21.909 --> 00:22:26.049
She says “Beware the beast beneath the boards”.

00:22:26.049 --> 00:22:29.929
This evokes dangerous hidden forces at the
Red Keep like Larys and Mysaria with their

00:22:29.929 --> 00:22:32.869
spies and rats in the secret tunnels.

00:22:32.869 --> 00:22:38.200
And metaphorically, the beast beneath the
boards could be the conflict and resentment

00:22:38.200 --> 00:22:42.629
that still lurks beneath this appearance of
peace.

00:22:42.629 --> 00:22:48.169
Helaena gives a speech about how her marriage
with Aegon isn’t so bad cause Aegon mostly

00:22:48.169 --> 00:22:49.539
ignores her.

00:22:49.539 --> 00:22:54.500
Which is dark, but it’s also the longest
coherent speech we’ve seen from Helaena,

00:22:54.500 --> 00:22:57.919
and Otto is proud of his granddaughter.

00:22:57.919 --> 00:23:02.130
Turns out even Otto is capable of being nice
sometimes.

00:23:02.130 --> 00:23:08.360
Jace dances with Helaena, and their goofy
joy is about the most wholesome moment all

00:23:08.360 --> 00:23:09.360
season.

00:23:09.360 --> 00:23:13.090
Remember that Rhaenyra proposed for Jace to
marry Helaena.

00:23:13.090 --> 00:23:18.409
So this is a bittersweet vision of what could
have been if that marriage happened.

00:23:18.409 --> 00:23:23.639
Though at the same time, Jace dancing with
Helaena might be a subtle dig at Helaena’s

00:23:23.639 --> 00:23:29.419
husband Aegon as revenge for Aegon insulting
Baela – that’s more how it seems in the

00:23:29.419 --> 00:23:30.419
book, anyway.

00:23:30.419 --> 00:23:34.899
But the adults get along, and have a good
time, and for a moment it seems like there

00:23:34.899 --> 00:23:38.759
might be peace between Rhaenyra and Alicent’s
families.

00:23:38.759 --> 00:23:44.460
So Viserys goes to bed believing that he’s
done the right thing, and everything’s gonna

00:23:44.460 --> 00:23:45.989
be okay.

00:23:45.989 --> 00:23:47.619
And then everything goes wrong.

00:23:47.619 --> 00:23:51.289
A servant puts a roast pig in front of Aemond.

00:23:51.289 --> 00:23:52.960
And Luke laughs.

00:23:52.960 --> 00:23:57.200
Because previously, Luke gave Aemond a pig
to bully him.

00:23:57.200 --> 00:23:58.200
And Luke is the one who cut out Aemond’s
eye last episode.

00:23:58.200 --> 00:24:01.989
So Aemond is furious, and he gives a subtly
insulting speech.

00:24:01.989 --> 00:24:08.109
He says Jace and Luke are “Strong boys”,
which sounds like a compliment, but really

00:24:08.109 --> 00:24:11.899
he’s saying that they are Harwin Strong’s
bastard sons.

00:24:11.899 --> 00:24:17.429
So the boys fight, until Daemon ends the scuffle
with one finger.

00:24:17.429 --> 00:24:23.289
Daemon stares down Aemond, and he wins the
staring contest cause he has twice as many

00:24:23.289 --> 00:24:24.289
eyes.

00:24:24.289 --> 00:24:30.200
It looks these Aemond and Daemon would love
to fight, or make out, or something.

00:24:30.200 --> 00:24:34.519
Aemond seems to both idolize Daemon and see
him as a rival.

00:24:34.519 --> 00:24:39.029
When Daemon killed Vaemond, Aemond looked
inspired.

00:24:39.029 --> 00:24:42.820
Rhaenyra and Alicent hold hands and try to
be friends again.

00:24:42.820 --> 00:24:47.499
But these mothers have passed their conflict
down to their children, and the children have

00:24:47.499 --> 00:24:49.729
not let go of this rivalry.

00:24:49.729 --> 00:24:54.929
The book says that just “The sins of the
fathers” are visited on sons, and “the

00:24:54.929 --> 00:24:57.609
sins of mothers” are as well.

00:24:57.609 --> 00:25:03.039
Can Rhaenyra and Alicent undo the damage of
their past conflict?

00:25:03.039 --> 00:25:05.830
We see Mysaria meet with Talya.

00:25:05.830 --> 00:25:10.309
Mysaria was Daemon’s lover, and has now
become a spymaster.

00:25:10.309 --> 00:25:13.739
Talya is Alicent’s maid in the Red Keep.

00:25:13.739 --> 00:25:17.200
And now it seems that Talya is spying for
Mysaria.

00:25:17.200 --> 00:25:20.110
So what is Mysaria up to?

00:25:20.110 --> 00:25:22.440
Previously Mysaria spied for Otto.

00:25:22.440 --> 00:25:28.299
Is Mysaria still working for Otto, or is she
maybe working for Larys now?

00:25:28.299 --> 00:25:33.229
Are Mysaria’s child spies listening from
the secret passages in the Red Keep, and that’s

00:25:33.229 --> 00:25:35.219
how Larys knows things?

00:25:35.219 --> 00:25:37.809
Or is Mysaria working for herself?

00:25:37.809 --> 00:25:41.389
Maybe she wants revenge on Daemon for him
abandoning her.

00:25:41.389 --> 00:25:42.830
Is Mysaria the beast beneath the boards that
Helaena mentioned?

00:25:42.830 --> 00:25:43.830
Viserys is dying.

00:25:43.830 --> 00:25:47.179
He’s in pain, he’s heavily drugged.

00:25:47.179 --> 00:25:51.869
So he speaks to Alicent, but Viserys thinks
he’s speaking to Rhaenyra.

00:25:51.869 --> 00:25:57.799
He tries to continue his earlier conversation
with Rhaenyra about Aegon’s dream, the prophecy

00:25:57.799 --> 00:26:01.700
that the Targaryens must unite to save Westeros.

00:26:01.700 --> 00:26:04.470
Alicent doesn’t know about this prophecy.

00:26:04.470 --> 00:26:09.289
But she hears Viserys say “Aegon” and
“You must do this”, so Alicent thinks

00:26:09.289 --> 00:26:12.899
Viserys wants her to make their son Aegon
king.

00:26:12.899 --> 00:26:19.239
That’s not what Viserys means – Viserys
barely remembers his son Aegon exists.

00:26:19.239 --> 00:26:24.549
What Viserys actually means is that Rhaenyra
is the prince that was promised – that Rhaenyra

00:26:24.549 --> 00:26:29.299
is the saviour who will unite the realm and
defeat the white walkers.

00:26:29.299 --> 00:26:31.590
And we know that’s not true.

00:26:31.590 --> 00:26:36.039
The white walkers don’t actually turn up
until a hundred and seventy years later in

00:26:36.039 --> 00:26:37.419
Game of Thrones.

00:26:37.419 --> 00:26:40.749
But this is a classic Targaryen mistake.

00:26:40.749 --> 00:26:46.259
Several generations of Targaryens have believed
that they will be the heroes to save the world,

00:26:46.259 --> 00:26:47.769
but been wrong.

00:26:47.769 --> 00:26:52.169
Rhaegar Targaryen believes himself to the
prince that was promised, but then he changes

00:26:52.169 --> 00:26:55.570
his mind and says his son is the saviour.

00:26:55.570 --> 00:27:00.309
Aemon Targaryen on his deathbed says that
Daenerys is the prince that was promised.

00:27:00.309 --> 00:27:04.609
Aegon the Conqueror, who started this prophecy,
thought that he would be the one to beat the

00:27:04.609 --> 00:27:09.849
white walkers – at least according to the
showrunner of Hot D, that detail isn’t in

00:27:09.849 --> 00:27:10.849
the books.

00:27:10.849 --> 00:27:15.909
But this is one of the dangers of prophecy
– people assume that they or their children

00:27:15.909 --> 00:27:21.210
are the most important people in the world,
at that can lead to disaster.

00:27:21.210 --> 00:27:27.429
Alicent wrongly believes that Viserys’ dying
wish is for Aegon to be king – even though

00:27:27.429 --> 00:27:33.519
Alicent just said she supports Rhaenyra, and
told Aegon that her not her son.

00:27:33.519 --> 00:27:38.769
But maybe on some level Alicent wants to believe
this.

00:27:38.769 --> 00:27:44.029
Because Alicent and Otto have spent years
building political strength for their family.

00:27:44.029 --> 00:27:50.080
And Alicent’s resentment of Rhaenyra for
her lies and infidelity have not gone away.

00:27:50.080 --> 00:27:57.899
So a dangerous mix of emotion ambition prophecy
and confusion is swirling through Alicent’s

00:27:57.899 --> 00:27:58.899
mind.

00:27:58.899 --> 00:28:04.519
When it’s time to decide who gets the Throne,
who will Alicent choose?

00:28:04.519 --> 00:28:08.149
Alicent leaves, and the king dies alone.

00:28:08.149 --> 00:28:12.289
Viserys says “No more”, and “My love”.

00:28:12.289 --> 00:28:15.629
His love is Aemma, his first wife.

00:28:15.629 --> 00:28:21.330
Viserys’ actor says Viserys never stops
loving Aemma, and sees Aemma’s face as he

00:28:21.330 --> 00:28:27.140
dies.The phrase “No more” might refer
to Aemma saying she won’t birth any more

00:28:27.140 --> 00:28:28.140
children.

00:28:28.140 --> 00:28:33.580
Viserys’ insistence on impregnating Aemma
despite the health risks got Aemma killed,

00:28:33.580 --> 00:28:36.369
and Viserys still feels guilty for that.

00:28:36.369 --> 00:28:41.799
“No more” might also mean Viserys will
feel “No more” pain – he has suffered

00:28:41.799 --> 00:28:48.619
so much, but now that he.. thinks that everything
will be fine, maybe Viserys welcomes death.

00:28:48.619 --> 00:28:53.020
In a way, he’s been dead ever since Aemma
died.

00:28:53.020 --> 00:28:58.190
This whole first season of House of the Dragon
has basically been just backstory.

00:28:58.190 --> 00:29:04.019
This is the prologue, the setup, the building
of tension before the main event.

00:29:04.019 --> 00:29:09.559
Now that King Viserys is dead, and now that
we know these characters and their relationships,

00:29:09.559 --> 00:29:12.649
the real conflict can begin.

00:29:12.649 --> 00:29:17.989
If you wanna know the full story of Hot D,
you’ve gotta check out the book, Fire &amp; Blood.

00:29:17.989 --> 00:29:22.340
There’s also the main series of Game of
Thrones books, and the worldbook, and Dunk

00:29:22.340 --> 00:29:23.340
&amp; Egg.

00:29:23.340 --> 00:29:29.289
You can get any one of these on audiobook
for free right now at audible.com/asx.

